      children: "A large retail bank replaced its core banking system using a Water-Scrum-Fall hybrid. The 18-month project had 3 months of upfront requirements and architecture (Waterfall), 12 months of Scrum development (15 teams, 120 developers, 2-week sprints), and 3 months of system integration and regulatory testing (Waterfall). Of 2,500 requirements, 92% were delivered in the first release. The project was delivered 2 months late but within budget due to careful scope management."
